HR for Greater Good: SECL Director (HR) Shri Biranchi Das joins panel discussion on Labour Reforms at XLRI Jamshedpur

SECL Director (HR) Shri Biranchi Das participated in a panel discussion on “Labour Reforms & Its Implications for Labour Relations: Industrial Relations” at the HR for Greater Good Conclave, being held at XLRI, Jamshedpur, from 31 August to 2 September 2026.

The conclave brings together leading HR professionals, industry experts and thought leaders to deliberate on emerging trends and contemporary challenges in human resource management and industrial relations.

During the panel discussion, Shri Biranchi Das shared his perspectives on the evolving labour reforms landscape and its implications for industrial relations, workplace practices and harmonious labour-management relations.

The session was moderated by Prof. Paramjyot Singh, XLRI Jamshedpur.

